<!-- The vawb motion-brief Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points;
     the W.D. Va. rules set no typeface or size, 12 pt is the filed motion's); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes
     (typst pitch-body, double spaced as filed) with no first-line indent (typst first-line-indent 0), the headings on
     the same pitch with no space of their own (typst: heading blocks above and below 0); single lines in 13.8 pt
     boxes (typst pitch-single); footnotes at 10 pt in 11.5 pt boxes, 6 pt apart (typst note-size, pitch-note,
     note-gap). Added or replaced here, as the typst template sets them: Body Text without an indent, "Numbered
     Paragraph" (the number half an inch in, a tab to 1 in, the text wrapped at 1 in; typst number-indent,
     number-box) and its "Note" variant (no widow control, for a paragraph that anchors a footnote), Heading 1 (bold,
     centred) and Heading 2 to 5 (the typed I. / A. / 1. / a. label, a tab to 0.5 in, the text hanging there; typst
     label-box; 2 and 3 bold, 4 italic, 5 plain), Footnote Text (the recipe's, without keepLines: typst splits a long
     note across pages), and the footer: the page number centred at 10 pt in an 11.5 pt line box (typst footer-size,
     pitch-footer) whose foot is 38.9 pt above the page edge (footer="778": 72 pt margin - 21.6 pt typst
     footer-descent 30 % - 11.5 pt). The section: letter, top margin 1.5 in (LR 5005-3(C), LR 7001-1(C)(3)), other
     margins 1 in. Caption, signature block and certificate of service carry their own spacing
     (docx/vawb-motion-brief.lua). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
